#!/bin/sh
# cl-stack-code as a command for agent-eval's adapter, from the cl-stack-code
# package cl-repo installed (harness-demos-eval depends on it). The demo passes
# its own image's source registry as CL_SOURCE_REGISTRY in the adapter's env:
# `cl-repo run` configures the Lisp it starts but exports no registry. Arguments pass through to
# CL-STACK-CODE:RUN-CLI, the entry point of the cl-stack-code binary
# (SBCL leaves only the arguments after --end-toplevel-options in *posix-argv*).
exec sbcl --noinform --non-interactive --no-sysinit --no-userinit \
  --eval '(require "asdf")' \
  --eval '(let ((*standard-output* *error-output*)) (asdf:load-system "cl-stack-code"))' \
  --eval '(uiop:quit (funcall (uiop:find-symbol* "RUN-CLI" "CL-STACK-CODE") (rest sb-ext:*posix-argv*)))' \
  --end-toplevel-options "$@"
